son":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/941cf64f683b87a07cf7a7b5a6c11b1188a763c0","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/commit/941cf64f683b87a07cf7a7b5a6c11b1188a763c0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/941cf64f683b87a07cf7a7b5a6c11b1188a763c0/comments","author":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"cdbf125200ba43c7b2460cff74f3318460e7f108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/cdbf125200ba43c7b2460cff74f3318460e7f108","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/commit/cdbf125200ba43c7b2460cff74f3318460e7f108"}]},{"sha":"6cd52cec203047eac723bcafbf6e154682b06318","node_id":"C_kwDOTfIvP9oAKDZjZDUyY2VjMjAzMDQ3ZWFjNzIzYmNhZmJmNmUxNTQ2ODJiMDYzMTg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alec Kriebel","email":"me@aleckriebel.com","date":"2026-08-07T04:10:02Z"},"committer":{"name":"Alec Kriebel","email":"me@aleckriebel.com","date":"2026-08-07T04:10:02Z"},"message":"Publish stronger author-ready releases for both unlisted papers\n\nReplaces both previously published papers with much stronger, submission-\nready versions supplied by the author, reconciling in place.\n\ns_tc_jc_sharp_boundary/ (version 1.1.1): the old flat release is now\nbyte-identical to reproducibility/exact_release/ inside a full journal\nsubmission package. The headline theorem is strictly stronger: a new\nautomatic-triangle-bound theorem proves every binary W_TC level-2 topology\nhas at most one triangle per blob, removing the triangle-count hypothesis\nentirely, so the classification now covers all binary standard\nsemi-directed S_TC level-2 networks. Adds the 48-page journal manuscript\n(source/paper/), a prior-work comparison against Ardiyansyah (2021) and\nEnglander et al. (2025), submission materials (referee guide, cover\nletters), and a new publication/ certificate layer (automatic-triangle\ncensus, regenerated cycle/theta atlases through seven ports). Independently\nreran verify_integrity.py, verify_multitriangle_exclusion.py,\nverify_base_release_attestation.py, review_publication_release.py, the\noriginal exact_release verifier, and a locally compiled independent C++\ncensus: all passed (reproducibility/GIT_MIRROR_VERIFICATION.txt). Two files\nare omitted from this git mirror for hosting-size reasons (redundant zip\narchives and a 175 MB exhaustive signature dump used only by the optional\nfull-regeneration path); see the note added to README.md.\n\nbimolecular_positive_recurrence/ (adds version 0.2 author-ready layer):\nthe full Phase I-V discovery history already committed here is preserved\nunmodified. Adds an independent Gate A1-A12 adversarial reconstruction of\nthe proof, arXiv and Journal of Applied Probability manuscript wrappers, a\ndependency-free standalone verifier package, and a narrow priority audit\nshowing this removes the pure-species-complex hypothesis of Anderson,\nCappelletti, and Kim (2020) and proves nonexplosion directly rather than\ninheriting it. Independently reran the 19-test suite and the byte-\nreproducible verification report twice (code/GIT_MIRROR_VERIFICATION.txt):\nidentical SHA-256 output on both runs, matching the released report.\n\nBoth docs/papers/ pages are rewritten to reflect the stronger results and\nlink to the new certificates, verifiers, and submission materials; both\nremain intentionally unlinked from the site homepage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"808054451fa3d03f500ba6ae431e8692370d847a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/git/trees/808054451fa3d03f500ba6ae431e8692370d847a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/git/commits/6cd52cec203047eac723bcafbf6e154682b06318","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/6cd52cec203047eac723bcafbf6e154682b06318","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/commit/6cd52cec203047eac723bcafbf6e154682b06318","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/6cd52cec203047eac723bcafbf6e154682b06318/comments","author":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/commit/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc"}]},{"sha":"b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","node_id":"C_kwDOTfIvP9oAKGI2ZmQ4MTczMTMzNTdjMTMzMzJlMDlmMmE4NTJjYmQ4NTEwMzJkZmM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Alec Kriebel","email":"me@aleckriebel.com","date":"2026-08-06T13:49:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"Alec Kriebel","email":"me@aleckriebel.com","date":"2026-08-06T13:49:13Z"},"message":"Add sharp S_TC/W_TC JC boundary and bimolecular positive-recurrence papers\n\nPublishes two new results as unlisted paper pages, following the existing\npattern of committing source alongside a public page not linked from the\nhomepage:\n\n- s_tc_jc_sharp_boundary/: a complete one-sided observational classification\n  for binary standard semi-directed S_TC level-2 phylogenetic networks under\n  the Jukes-Cantor model (generic identifiability modulo ordinary triangle\n  redirection T), with a matching all-n sharpness counterexample on\n  W_TC \\ S_TC. Rerun `python3 verify_release.py` end to end in a fresh\n  Python 3.14.6 / SymPy virtual environment: ALL EXACT CHECKS PASSED.\n\n- bimolecular_positive_recurrence/: positive recurrence of every finite\n  one-linkage-class bimolecular weakly reversible stochastic mass-action\n  network, for every positive rate vector, via a target/source\n  residual-factorial Foster function. The full discovery history (failed\n  lemmas and phases II-IV) is preserved alongside the Phase V\n  self-contained final proof. Reran the Phase V test suite and independent\n  verifier fresh; all 11 tests passed and every module self-test returned 0.\n  Rerun transcript archived at bimolecular_positive_recurrence/\n  verification_transcript.txt.\n\nPaper pages at docs/papers/s-tc-jc-sharp-boundary/ and\ndocs/papers/bimolecular-positive-recurrence/ are intentionally not linked\nfrom the site homepage, with top-level buttons to the verifier, the\ncertificates directories, and (for the bimolecular paper) Phase V\nspecifically.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ecb7abc3071ff5c30844eba07cf0faa3538651af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/git/trees/ecb7abc3071ff5c30844eba07cf0faa3538651af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/git/commits/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/commit/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AlecKriebel/Math/commits/b6fd817313357c13332e09f2a852cbd851032dfc/comments","author":{"login":"AlecKriebel","id":6109370,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6109370?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel","html_url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlecKriebel/received_events","type":"User","user_view